{"t":"2026-05-20T20:14:54.052Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012NYAjztqozF6S11RF3YYwj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# CLAUDE.md — Talent Agent\n     2→## VibeSpace LLC · Built by Space Cowboy #9\n     3→\n     4→---\n     5→\n     6→## WHO YOU ARE\n     7→\n     8→You are a senior AI engineer working inside the **Talent Agent** project — part of the **Digital Renaissance ecosystem** built by **VibeSpace LLC (\"The Dot Connector\")**, founded by **Sean Young (Space Cowboy #9)** in Miami, FL.\n     9→\n    10→You operate with the autonomy of a principal engineer. You make architectural decisions, write production-grade code, handle edge cases without being asked, and always think about the next step before the operator asks for it. You are not a code generator — you are a builder.\n    11→\n    12→---\n    13→\n    14→## OPERATOR\n    15→\n    16→**Sean Young** (goes by SPY, \"Space Cowboy #9\")\n    17→Founder & CEO, VibeSpace LLC\n    18→Principal AI Engineer · Systems Architect\n    19→Miami, FL · github.com/tyzeeington · spy@seanyoung.biz\n    20→\n    21→**Background:** 7+ years enterprise fintech engineering (JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America). Expert in Java/Spring Boot, Python/FastAPI, distributed systems, microservices, Kubernetes, and AI systems. Now building the Digital Renaissance — an interconnected ecosystem of AI-powered platforms.\n    22→\n    23→**Preferences:**\n    24→- Prefers working fast and iterating — ship a working version, then improve\n    25→- Does not want excessive explanation of obvious things — just build it\n    26→- Wants clean, readable code over clever code\n    27→- Values modularity — every component should be replaceable\n    28→- Dislikes over-engineering — solve the problem in front of you, not hypothetical future problems\n    29→- Prefers Python for AI/agent work, FastAPI as the standard backend\n    30→- Async first — everything that touches I/O should be async\n    31→\n    32→---\n    33→\n    34→## PROJECT OVERVIEW\n    35→\n    36→**Talent Agent** is a 24/7 autonomous AI talent system that discovers real jobs from Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, and Workday public boards, tailors resumes with AI, researches target companies, composes personalized outreach, and submits real applications to live ATS systems—all orchestrated through a React 19 + Vite frontend and FastAPI backend with PostgreSQL persistence.\n    37→\n    38→**Initial use case:** Single candidate (Sean Young) using his own resume to test and validate the system.\n    39→\n    40→**Target market:** Recruiting agencies managing 50–500 candidates simultaneously.\n    41→\n    42→---\n    43→\n    44→## Stack\n    45→- Frontend: React 19 · Vite 8 · Tailwind 4 · lucide-react · react-router-dom 7\n    46→- Backend: FastAPI · Python 3.12 · Pydantic v2 · SQLAlchemy 2.0 async · Alembic\n    47→- DB: PostgreSQL 15 (raw, via SQLAlchemy async engine)\n    48→- Auth: JWT HS256 (7d, localStorage) + Magic-link via Resend\n    49→- Storage: Local FS (dev) / S3 (prod future)\n    50→- AI: Claude API (`claude-sonnet-4-20250514`) · Anthropic Python SDK\n    51→- Observability: structlog + Redis pub/sub\n    52→- Infrastructure: Docker · AWS ECS Fargate (us-east-1) · ECR · Digital Dash pipeline\n    53→\n    54→**Type stack:** Playfair Display (serif) · DM Sans (sans) · DM Mono (mono). Icon system: lucide-react only.\n    55→\n    56→---\n    57→\n    58→## Stream Convention\n    59→\n    60→- **Stream tag:** `TA/`\n    61→- **Branch:** `TA/<kebab-desc>`\n    62→- **Commit subject:** `[TA] <imperative>`\n    63→- **PR title:** `[TA] <what shipped>`\n    64→\n    65→Format: `MF/DOMAIN: description` where DOMAIN matches a biome (e.g., `MF/AUTH: wire Resend magic-link send`).\n    66→\n    67→---\n    68→\n    69→## Active HYPHA\n    70→\n    71→See `hyphae/HYPHA-{DOMAIN}.md` for the frozen contract of each biome:\n    72→\n    73→| Tag | File | Responsibility |\n    74→|---|---|---|\n    75→| `TA/SCHEMA` | `hyphae/HYPHA-SCHEMA-CORE.md` | Data contracts — migrations, ORM, Pydantic |\n    76→| `TA/DESIGN` | `hyphae/HYPHA-DESIGN-CORE.md` | Design tokens, Top Shelf editorial |\n    77→| `TA/AUTH` | `hyphae/HYPHA-AUTH.md` | JWT, magic-link, Resend |\n    78→| `TA/ONBOARD` | `hyphae/HYPHA-ONBOARDING.md` | Resume upload, profile capture |\n    79→| `TA/DISCOVER` | `hyphae/HYPHA-DISCOVERY-ENGINE.md` | Multi-source job crawler |\n    80→| `TA/APPLY` | `hyphae/HYPHA-APPLICATION-ENGINE.md` | AutoApply Playwright engine |\n    81→| `TA/AGENTS` | `hyphae/HYPHA-AGENT-MANAGER.md` | Claude tool_use agentic layer |\n    82→| `TA/API` | `hyphae/HYPHA-API-SURFACE.md` | FastAPI app, routers, /health |\n    83→| `TA/DASH` | `hyphae/HYPHA-REVIEW-DASHBOARD.md` | React frontend, auth flow |\n    84→| `TA/OBS` | `hyphae/HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md` | Logging, pub/sub, health |\n    85→| `TA/INFRA` | `hyphae/HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY.md` | Docker, ECS, Digital Dash |\n    86→\n    87→---\n    88→\n    89→## Contracts\n    90→\n    91→See `NUTRIENTS.md` for frozen contract surfaces including:\n    92→- **DATA_CONTRACTS** — TypeScript interfaces for all domain entities\n    93→- **DESIGN_TOKENS** — Color palette, typography, spacing (Top Shelf editorial)\n    94→- **API_CONTRACTS** — Full request/response shapes per endpoint\n    95→- **Section H** — Security rules (stack-canon overrides apply)\n    96→\n    97→---\n    98→\n    99→## Rules\n   100→\n   101→### Stack Canon (READ FIRST)\n   102→\n   103→This repo uses `--stack nextjs-fastapi-supabase` as a fallback—there is no `fastapi-postgres` preset. **The preset's contract appendix Section H is wrong for this stack** in three ways:\n   104→\n   105→**Negated rules (do NOT enforce):**\n   106→- **H.1.3** — Uses `VITE_*` prefix, NOT `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` (Vite, not Next.js)\n   107→- **H.2.1** — JWT in localStorage, NOT httpOnly cookies\n   108→- **H.3.1** — Raw PostgreSQL via SQLAlchemy, NOT Supabase RLS\n   109→\n   110→**Positive canon:**\n   111→- Frontend: React 19 · Vite 8 · Tailwind 4. Pages at `frontend/src/pages/*.jsx`, components at `frontend/src/components/*.jsx`\n   112→- Backend: FastAPI · Python 3.12 · Pydantic v2 · SQLAlchemy 2.0 async. Routes at `backend/api/*.py` under `/api/v1`\n   113→- Database: PostgreSQL 15 via SQLAlchemy async in `backend/database.py`. Migrations at `backend/migrations/`\n   114→- Auth: JWT HS256, 7d, stored in localStorage, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n   115→- Env vars: `VITE_*` for frontend (`import.meta.env`), unprefixed for backend (`backend/config.py`)\n   116→\n   117→### Development\n   118→\n   119→- FastAPI only for backend — no Express, no other framework\n   120→- All DB access via SQLAlchemy async — no raw SQL outside migrations\n   121→- Design tokens from `NUTRIENTS.md` → `DESIGN_TOKENS` — no hardcoded colors or fonts\n   122→- Mobile-first — every component built for mobile, scaled up to desktop\n   123→- TypeScript strict mode — no `any`\n   124→- Dark theme is default and only\n   125→- No `print()` — use structlog\n   126→- No `requests` — use httpx\n   127→- No bare `except:` — always specify exception type\n   128→- Type hints on every function and class\n   129→- Docstrings on every class and public method\n   130→- Pydantic v2 for all data models\n   131→\n   132→### Database\n   133→\n   134→- SQLAlchemy 2.0 async ORM\n   135→- Alembic for all schema changes — never modify tables manually\n   136→- Every table has: `id UUID PK`, `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ`, `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ`\n   137→- Use transactions for multi-step writes\n   138→\n   139→### Claude API Calls\n   140→\n   141→- Always use `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`\n   142→- `max_tokens: 4096` unless you need more\n   143→- Wrap in retry logic — 3 attempts, exponential backoff\n   144→- Log prompt + response for every call (redact PII in logs)\n   145→- Cache responses in Redis where appropriate (keyed by content hash)\n   146→\n   147→### External Scraping\n   148→\n   149→- Respect `robots.txt`\n   150→- Rate limit: 1–2 req/sec per domain\n   151→- Randomised delay 0.5–2.0s between requests\n   152→- User-agent: identify as a bot (`VibeSpaceTalentAgent/1.0`)\n   153→- If 429 or 503: exponential backoff, max 3 retries, then log and skip\n   154→\n   155→### Security\n   156→\n   157→- No hardcoded secrets in committed code\n   158→- `.env` gitignored; only `.env.example` committed\n   159→- Secrets in AWS Secrets Manager for prod\n   160→- PII redaction in Claude prompt/response logs\n   161→\n   162→### Git\n   163→\n   164→- No `git` from leaves — `./auto-commit.sh` only\n   165→- `git push --force` / `rm -rf` outside `/tmp` require explicit confirmation\n   166→- Apache 2.0 header on every new file\n   167→\n   168→### Cultivation\n   169→\n   170→- Run with `--skip-audit` (preset rules conflict with actual stack)\n   171→- Concurrency: `-c 4` (not 30 — rate limit discipline)\n   172→- Real ATS submissions require human approval — no automated bypass\n   173→\n   174→---\n   175→\n   176→## PROJECT STRUCTURE\n   177→\n   178→```\n   179→talent-agent/\n   180→├── CLAUDE.md                    ← you are here\n   181→├── mycelium.yaml                ← organism config for cultivation\n   182→├── NUTRIENTS.md                 ← frozen contracts\n   183→├── CELLULAR-MAP.md              ← execution tree + concurrency map\n   184→├── README.md\n   185→├── hyphae/                      ← per-biome contracts (11 frozen)\n   186→│   ├── HYPHA-SCHEMA-CORE.md\n   187→│   ├── HYPHA-DESIGN-CORE.md\n   188→│   ├── HYPHA-AUTH.md\n   189→│   ├── HYPHA-ONBOARDING.md\n   190→│   ├── HYPHA-DISCOVERY-ENGINE.md\n   191→│   ├── HYPHA-APPLICATION-ENGINE.md\n   192→│   ├── HYPHA-AGENT-MANAGER.md\n   193→│   ├── HYPHA-API-SURFACE.md\n   194→│   ├── HYPHA-REVIEW-DASHBOARD.md\n   195→│   ├── HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md\n   196→│   └── HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY.md\n   197→├── agents/                      ← Mycelium agent stubs\n   198→├── backend/\n   199→│   ├── main.py                  ← FastAPI app entry\n   200→│   ├── config.py                ← settings from env\n   201→│   ├── database.py              ← async SQLAlchemy engine\n   202→│   ├── agents/\n   203→│   │   ├── discovery/           ← Discovery Engine\n   204→│   │   └── application/         ← Application Engine\n   205→│   ├── models/\n   206→│   ├── api/\n   207→│   └── migrations/\n   208→├── frontend/                    ← React 19 + Vite 8 + Tailwind 4\n   209→│   └── src/\n   210→├── tests/\n   211→├── deploy/\n   212→│   ├── deploy.sh\n   213→│   ├── setup-aws.sh\n   214→│   └── ecs-task-def-*.json\n   215→├── digital-dash-pipeline.yml\n   216→├── docker-compose.yml\n   217→├── .env.example\n   218→└── requirements.txt\n   219→```\n   220→\n   221→---\n   222→\n   223→## AGENT LIFECYCLE\n   224→\n   225→All agents follow this status state machine:\n   226→\n   227→```\n   228→QUEUED → RUNNING → COMPLETED\n   229→                 → FAILED → RETRYING → COMPLETED\n   230→                                     → DEAD\n   231→```\n   232→\n   233→Every status transition:\n   234→- Logged to PostgreSQL with timestamp\n   235→- Published on Redis pub/sub (`agent.status.{agent_name}`)\n   236→- Surfaced in the Review Dashboard\n   237→\n   238→---\n   239→\n   240→## NAMING CONVENTIONS\n   241→\n   242→| Thing | Convention | Example |\n   243→|---|---|---|\n   244→| Python files | `snake_case.py` | `identity_profiler.py` |\n   245→| Classes | `PascalCase` | `IdentityProfiler` |\n   246→| Functions | `snake_case` | `build_profile()` |\n   247→| DB tables | `snake_case` | `discovered_jobs` |\n   248→| Redis keys | `{namespace}:{entity}:{id}` | `digest:candidate:abc123` |\n   249→| Events | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `DIGEST_READY` |\n   250→| Env vars | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` |\n   251→\n   252→---\n   253→\n   254→## CURRENT PHASE\n   255→\n   256→**Phase 1 — MVP (single candidate)**\n   257→- Goal: Get the system working end-to-end for one candidate (Sean Young)\n   258→- Scope: Discovery Engine + Application Engine + Review Dashboard\n   259→- Done when: System finds a real job, tailors a real resume, composes a real email, fills a real form — all reviewed and approved by the operator\n   260→\n   261→**Do not over-engineer for multi-tenancy yet.** Design with multi-tenancy in mind (candidate_id as FK everywhere), but don't build the agency dashboard or white-label features yet. Validate the core loop first.\n   262→\n   263→---\n   264→\n   265→## AUTO-COMMIT RULE\n   266→\n   267→After completing any feature, fix, or meaningful unit of work:\n   268→\n   269→1. Run `./auto-commit.sh` from the project root\n   270→2. If the script doesn't exist, stop and notify the user — do NOT commit manually\n   271→3. Do NOT batch multiple features into one commit\n   272→4. Commit after EACH discrete task is complete\n   273→\n   274→**Custom message:** `./auto-commit.sh \"[TA] message\"`\n   275→**Auto-message:** `./auto-commit.sh` (detects scope + action from changed files)\n   276→\n   277→---\n   278→\n   279→*The Dot Connects.*\n   280→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"896edb10-d5e4-4e2d-8d2d-7fe02bdd0dae","uuid":"78df5037-3e72-4281-b8da-3c25220d0cde","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomation/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md — Talent Agent\n## VibeSpace LLC · Built by Space Cowboy #9\n\n---\n\n## WHO YOU ARE\n\nYou are a senior AI engineer working inside the **Talent Agent** project — part of the **Digital Renaissance ecosystem** built by **VibeSpace LLC (\"The Dot Connector\")**, founded by **Sean Young (Space Cowboy #9)** in Miami, FL.\n\nYou operate with the autonomy of a principal engineer. You make architectural decisions, write production-grade code, handle edge cases without being asked, and always think about the next step before the operator asks for it. You are not a code generator — you are a builder.\n\n---\n\n## OPERATOR\n\n**Sean Young** (goes by SPY, \"Space Cowboy #9\")\nFounder & CEO, VibeSpace LLC\nPrincipal AI Engineer · Systems Architect\nMiami, FL · github.com/tyzeeington · spy@seanyoung.biz\n\n**Background:** 7+ years enterprise fintech engineering (JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America). Expert in Java/Spring Boot, Python/FastAPI, distributed systems, microservices, Kubernetes, and AI systems. Now building the Digital Renaissance — an interconnected ecosystem of AI-powered platforms.\n\n**Preferences:**\n- Prefers working fast and iterating — ship a working version, then improve\n- Does not want excessive explanation of obvious things — just build it\n- Wants clean, readable code over clever code\n- Values modularity — every component should be replaceable\n- Dislikes over-engineering — solve the problem in front of you, not hypothetical future problems\n- Prefers Python for AI/agent work, FastAPI as the standard backend\n- Async first — everything that touches I/O should be async\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT OVERVIEW\n\n**Talent Agent** is a 24/7 autonomous AI talent system that discovers real jobs from Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, and Workday public boards, tailors resumes with AI, researches target companies, composes personalized outreach, and submits real applications to live ATS systems—all orchestrated through a React 19 + Vite frontend and FastAPI backend with PostgreSQL persistence.\n\n**Initial use case:** Single candidate (Sean Young) using his own resume to test and validate the system.\n\n**Target market:** Recruiting agencies managing 50–500 candidates simultaneously.\n\n---\n\n## Stack\n- Frontend: React 19 · Vite 8 · Tailwind 4 · lucide-react · react-router-dom 7\n- Backend: FastAPI · Python 3.12 · Pydantic v2 · SQLAlchemy 2.0 async · Alembic\n- DB: PostgreSQL 15 (raw, via SQLAlchemy async engine)\n- Auth: JWT HS256 (7d, localStorage) + Magic-link via Resend\n- Storage: Local FS (dev) / S3 (prod future)\n- AI: Claude API (`claude-sonnet-4-20250514`) · Anthropic Python SDK\n- Observability: structlog + Redis pub/sub\n- Infrastructure: Docker · AWS ECS Fargate (us-east-1) · ECR · Digital Dash pipeline\n\n**Type stack:** Playfair Display (serif) · DM Sans (sans) · DM Mono (mono). Icon system: lucide-react only.\n\n---\n\n## Stream Convention\n\n- **Stream tag:** `TA/`\n- **Branch:** `TA/<kebab-desc>`\n- **Commit subject:** `[TA] <imperative>`\n- **PR title:** `[TA] <what shipped>`\n\nFormat: `MF/DOMAIN: description` where DOMAIN matches a biome (e.g., `MF/AUTH: wire Resend magic-link send`).\n\n---\n\n## Active HYPHA\n\nSee `hyphae/HYPHA-{DOMAIN}.md` for the frozen contract of each biome:\n\n| Tag | File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|---|\n| `TA/SCHEMA` | `hyphae/HYPHA-SCHEMA-CORE.md` | Data contracts — migrations, ORM, Pydantic |\n| `TA/DESIGN` | `hyphae/HYPHA-DESIGN-CORE.md` | Design tokens, Top Shelf editorial |\n| `TA/AUTH` | `hyphae/HYPHA-AUTH.md` | JWT, magic-link, Resend |\n| `TA/ONBOARD` | `hyphae/HYPHA-ONBOARDING.md` | Resume upload, profile capture |\n| `TA/DISCOVER` | `hyphae/HYPHA-DISCOVERY-ENGINE.md` | Multi-source job crawler |\n| `TA/APPLY` | `hyphae/HYPHA-APPLICATION-ENGINE.md` | AutoApply Playwright engine |\n| `TA/AGENTS` | `hyphae/HYPHA-AGENT-MANAGER.md` | Claude tool_use agentic layer |\n| `TA/API` | `hyphae/HYPHA-API-SURFACE.md` | FastAPI app, routers, /health |\n| `TA/DASH` | `hyphae/HYPHA-REVIEW-DASHBOARD.md` | React frontend, auth flow |\n| `TA/OBS` | `hyphae/HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md` | Logging, pub/sub, health |\n| `TA/INFRA` | `hyphae/HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY.md` | Docker, ECS, Digital Dash |\n\n---\n\n## Contracts\n\nSee `NUTRIENTS.md` for frozen contract surfaces including:\n- **DATA_CONTRACTS** — TypeScript interfaces for all domain entities\n- **DESIGN_TOKENS** — Color palette, typography, spacing (Top Shelf editorial)\n- **API_CONTRACTS** — Full request/response shapes per endpoint\n- **Section H** — Security rules (stack-canon overrides apply)\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\n### Stack Canon (READ FIRST)\n\nThis repo uses `--stack nextjs-fastapi-supabase` as a fallback—there is no `fastapi-postgres` preset. **The preset's contract appendix Section H is wrong for this stack** in three ways:\n\n**Negated rules (do NOT enforce):**\n- **H.1.3** — Uses `VITE_*` prefix, NOT `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` (Vite, not Next.js)\n- **H.2.1** — JWT in localStorage, NOT httpOnly cookies\n- **H.3.1** — Raw PostgreSQL via SQLAlchemy, NOT Supabase RLS\n\n**Positive canon:**\n- Frontend: React 19 · Vite 8 · Tailwind 4. Pages at `frontend/src/pages/*.jsx`, components at `frontend/src/components/*.jsx`\n- Backend: FastAPI · Python 3.12 · Pydantic v2 · SQLAlchemy 2.0 async. Routes at `backend/api/*.py` under `/api/v1`\n- Database: PostgreSQL 15 via SQLAlchemy async in `backend/database.py`. Migrations at `backend/migrations/`\n- Auth: JWT HS256, 7d, stored in localStorage, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n- Env vars: `VITE_*` for frontend (`import.meta.env`), unprefixed for backend (`backend/config.py`)\n\n### Development\n\n- FastAPI only for backend — no Express, no other framework\n- All DB access via SQLAlchemy async — no raw SQL outside migrations\n- Design tokens from `NUTRIENTS.md` → `DESIGN_TOKENS` — no hardcoded colors or fonts\n- Mobile-first — every component built for mobile, scaled up to desktop\n- TypeScript strict mode — no `any`\n- Dark theme is default and only\n- No `print()` — use structlog\n- No `requests` — use httpx\n- No bare `except:` — always specify exception type\n- Type hints on every function and class\n- Docstrings on every class and public method\n- Pydantic v2 for all data models\n\n### Database\n\n- SQLAlchemy 2.0 async ORM\n- Alembic for all schema changes — never modify tables manually\n- Every table has: `id UUID PK`, `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ`, `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ`\n- Use transactions for multi-step writes\n\n### Claude API Calls\n\n- Always use `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`\n- `max_tokens: 4096` unless you need more\n- Wrap in retry logic — 3 attempts, exponential backoff\n- Log prompt + response for every call (redact PII in logs)\n- Cache responses in Redis where appropriate (keyed by content hash)\n\n### External Scraping\n\n- Respect `robots.txt`\n- Rate limit: 1–2 req/sec per domain\n- Randomised delay 0.5–2.0s between requests\n- User-agent: identify as a bot (`VibeSpaceTalentAgent/1.0`)\n- If 429 or 503: exponential backoff, max 3 retries, then log and skip\n\n### Security\n\n- No hardcoded secrets in committed code\n- `.env` gitignored; only `.env.example` committed\n- Secrets in AWS Secrets Manager for prod\n- PII redaction in Claude prompt/response logs\n\n### Git\n\n- No `git` from leaves — `./auto-commit.sh` only\n- `git push --force` / `rm -rf` outside `/tmp` require explicit confirmation\n- Apache 2.0 header on every new file\n\n### Cultivation\n\n- Run with `--skip-audit` (preset rules conflict with actual stack)\n- Concurrency: `-c 4` (not 30 — rate limit discipline)\n- Real ATS submissions require human approval — no automated bypass\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\n```\ntalent-agent/\n├── CLAUDE.md                    ← you are here\n├── mycelium.yaml                ← organism config for cultivation\n├── NUTRIENTS.md                 ← frozen contracts\n├── CELLULAR-MAP.md              ← execution tree + concurrency map\n├── README.md\n├── hyphae/                      ← per-biome contracts (11 frozen)\n│   ├── HYPHA-SCHEMA-CORE.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-DESIGN-CORE.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-AUTH.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-ONBOARDING.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-DISCOVERY-ENGINE.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-APPLICATION-ENGINE.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-AGENT-MANAGER.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-API-SURFACE.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-REVIEW-DASHBOARD.md\n│   ├── HYPHA-OBSERVABILITY.md\n│   └── HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY.md\n├── agents/                      ← Mycelium agent stubs\n├── backend/\n│   ├── main.py                  ← FastAPI app entry\n│   ├── config.py                ← settings from env\n│   ├── database.py              ← async SQLAlchemy engine\n│   ├── agents/\n│   │   ├── discovery/           ← Discovery Engine\n│   │   └── application/         ← Application Engine\n│   ├── models/\n│   ├── api/\n│   └── migrations/\n├── frontend/                    ← React 19 + Vite 8 + Tailwind 4\n│   └── src/\n├── tests/\n├── deploy/\n│   ├── deploy.sh\n│   ├── setup-aws.sh\n│   └── ecs-task-def-*.json\n├── digital-dash-pipeline.yml\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── .env.example\n└── requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n## AGENT LIFECYCLE\n\nAll agents follow this status state machine:\n\n```\nQUEUED → RUNNING → COMPLETED\n                 → FAILED → RETRYING → COMPLETED\n                                     → DEAD\n```\n\nEvery status transition:\n- Logged to PostgreSQL with timestamp\n- Published on Redis pub/sub (`agent.status.{agent_name}`)\n- Surfaced in the Review Dashboard\n\n---\n\n## NAMING CONVENTIONS\n\n| Thing | Convention | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Python files | `snake_case.py` | `identity_profiler.py` |\n| Classes | `PascalCase` | `IdentityProfiler` |\n| Functions | `snake_case` | `build_profile()` |\n| DB tables | `snake_case` | `discovered_jobs` |\n| Redis keys | `{namespace}:{entity}:{id}` | `digest:candidate:abc123` |\n| Events | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `DIGEST_READY` |\n| Env vars | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` |\n\n---\n\n## CURRENT PHASE\n\n**Phase 1 — MVP (single candidate)**\n- Goal: Get the system working end-to-end for one candidate (Sean Young)\n- Scope: Discovery Engine + Application Engine + Review Dashboard\n- Done when: System finds a real job, tailors a real resume, composes a real email, fills a real form — all reviewed and approved by the operator\n\n**Do not over-engineer for multi-tenancy yet.** Design with multi-tenancy in mind (candidate_id as FK everywhere), but don't build the agency dashboard or white-label features yet. Validate the core loop first.\n\n---\n\n## AUTO-COMMIT RULE\n\nAfter completing any feature, fix, or meaningful unit of work:\n\n1. Run `./auto-commit.sh` from the project root\n2. If the script doesn't exist, stop and notify the user — do NOT commit manually\n3. Do NOT batch multiple features into one commit\n4. Commit after EACH discrete task is complete\n\n**Custom message:** `./auto-commit.sh \"[TA] message\"`\n**Auto-message:** `./auto-commit.sh` (detects scope + action from changed files)\n\n---\n\n*The Dot Connects.*\n","numLines":280,"startLine":1,"totalLines":280}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-20T20:14:54.066Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HJ9NNuhnDeu5efpH4q7zRu","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY\n     2→\n     3→> HYPHA tag: `TA/INFRA`\n     4→\n     5→## Goal\n     6→\n     7→Own the containerization, local-dev orchestration, AWS deployment, and Digital Dash CI/CD pipeline for Talent Agent. From `make up` to `./deploy/deploy.sh prod backend <sha>` to the production health check.\n     8→\n     9→## Scope\n    10→\n    11→### In Scope\n    12→- Backend `Dockerfile` (multi-stage; final image runs uvicorn)\n    13→- Frontend `Dockerfile` + `nginx.conf` (builds React + serves `dist/`)\n    14→- `docker-compose.yml` — local dev stack (postgres + redis + backend + frontend)\n    15→- `Makefile` — common targets (`up`, `down`, `logs`, `seed`, `lint`, `test`)\n    16→- `start.sh` / `stop.sh` — opinionated dev wrappers\n    17→- `deploy/setup-aws.sh` — one-time bootstrap (ECR repos, ECS cluster, IAM, Secrets Manager entries)\n    18→- `deploy/deploy.sh` — service deploy + rollback for backend/frontend across local/staging/prod\n    19→- `deploy/ecs-task-def-backend.json` + `deploy/ecs-task-def-frontend.json` — Fargate task definitions\n    20→- `digital-dash-pipeline.yml` — pipeline spec (lint → test → build → deploy-staging → health-check → deploy-prod with manual gate)\n    21→- `.env.example` — env-var template\n    22→- `.dockerignore` (if present; create if missing)\n    23→\n    24→### Out of Scope\n    25→- Multi-region deployment (us-east-1 only)\n    26→- Blue/green or canary (rolling update via ECS service update)\n    27→- Database backups (RDS managed)\n    28→- TLS cert provisioning (assume ACM cert exists, wired in ALB)\n    29→- Container runtime alternatives (no Kubernetes; ECS Fargate only)\n    30→- Pipeline alternatives (no GitHub Actions / CircleCI — Digital Dash is the pipeline)\n    31→\n    32→## Inputs\n    33→\n    34→- api-surface: backend exposes port 8000, `/health` returns `{status: \"ok\", version}`\n    35→- review-dashboard: frontend builds to `dist/`, nginx serves on 80\n    36→- Brief §0 (Stack lock) and §12 (Digital Dash result codes)\n    37→- AWS Secrets Manager entries (out-of-band): `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`\n    38→\n    39→## Outputs (Deliverables)\n    40→\n    41→Existing files locked at HEAD:\n    42→- `Dockerfile`\n    43→- `frontend/Dockerfile`\n    44→- `frontend/nginx.conf`\n    45→- `docker-compose.yml`\n    46→- `Makefile`\n    47→- `start.sh`, `stop.sh`\n    48→- `.env.example`\n    49→- `deploy/setup-aws.sh`\n    50→- `deploy/deploy.sh`\n    51→- `deploy/ecs-task-def-backend.json`\n    52→- `deploy/ecs-task-def-frontend.json`\n    53→- `digital-dash-pipeline.yml`\n    54→- `auto-commit.sh` (referenced as the per-task commit gate)\n    55→\n    56→## Acceptance Criteria\n    57→\n    58→### Local\n    59→- [ ] `docker-compose up -d` brings up postgres, redis, backend, frontend with healthy containers\n    60→- [ ] `make up` is equivalent to `docker-compose up -d`\n    61→- [ ] `make down` stops all services cleanly\n    62→- [ ] `make seed` runs `backend/seed.py` against the local DB\n    63→- [ ] `make logs` tails container logs\n    64→- [ ] Backend reaches `GET /health` returning `{status: \"ok\", …}` within 30s of `make up`\n    65→- [ ] Frontend reaches `http://localhost:5173` and renders Landing\n    66→\n    67→### Docker images\n    68→- [ ] Backend `Dockerfile` is multi-stage; runtime image is sub-500MB and runs as non-root\n    69→- [ ] Backend image starts uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` by default\n    70→- [ ] Frontend `Dockerfile` builds the React app with `npm ci && npm run build`, copies `dist/` into nginx, serves at port 80\n    71→- [ ] Frontend nginx config falls back to `index.html` for unmatched routes (SPA history routing)\n    72→\n    73→### AWS / ECS\n    74→- [ ] `deploy/setup-aws.sh` runs idempotently — re-running does not duplicate ECR repos or IAM roles\n    75→- [ ] ECR repos `talent-agent-backend` and `talent-agent-frontend` exist after bootstrap\n    76→- [ ] ECS cluster `vibespace-prod` exists with services `talent-agent-backend` and `talent-agent-frontend`\n    77→- [ ] Task definitions pull `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL` from AWS Secrets Manager (no plaintext secrets in JSON)\n    78→- [ ] `./deploy/deploy.sh staging backend <git-sha>` builds, pushes to ECR, registers a new task def revision, updates the ECS service, waits for the deployment to stabilize\n    79→- [ ] `./deploy/deploy.sh prod backend --rollback` reverts the service to the previous task def revision\n    80→- [ ] `./deploy/deploy.sh local` is a `docker-compose up` shortcut\n    81→\n    82→### Digital Dash pipeline\n    83→- [ ] `digital-dash-pipeline.yml` validates as YAML\n    84→- [ ] Stages run in order: `lint` → `test` → `build` → `deploy-staging` → `health-check` → `deploy-prod`\n    85→- [ ] `lint` runs `ruff check backend/`, `ruff format backend/ --check`, frontend `npm run lint`, and `bandit -ll` / `safety check` (warn-only)\n    86→- [ ] `test` provisions postgres + redis services and runs `pytest tests/`\n    87→- [ ] `build` is gated to `main` and `release/*` branches\n    88→- [ ] `deploy-prod` requires manual approval from `spy@seanyoung.biz` with 24h timeout\n    89→- [ ] `verify-prod` triggers an auto-rollback (backend + frontend) if `/health` is not `ok` post-deploy\n    90→- [ ] Green pipeline auto-merges; red flags for human review; warned passes notify\n    91→\n    92→### Auto-commit\n    93→- [ ] `./auto-commit.sh \"[TA] message\"` stages tracked changes, creates a commit prefixed with the stream tag, and refuses to commit secrets (`.env`, `credentials.json`)\n    94→- [ ] `./auto-commit.sh` with no args auto-detects scope from changed files\n    95→\n    96→## Notes\n    97→\n    98→- The `vibespace-prod` ECS cluster is shared across VibeSpace products. Service names are product-scoped (`talent-agent-backend`, `talent-agent-frontend`).\n    99→- Region is `us-east-1` everywhere. Changing region requires a brief amendment.\n   100→- Secrets must NEVER appear in task definition JSON in plaintext — always `valueFrom` ARNs to Secrets Manager.\n   101→- `health-check` stage uses `${STAGING_URL}` and a 5×10s retry pattern. Don't shorten the retry window — staging cold-start can take 30+ seconds.\n   102→- `deploy-prod` manual gate is non-negotiable for this cultivation. Auto-merging to production without an approver is out of scope.\n   103→- Rollback strategy: deploy.sh stores the previous task def revision; rollback re-registers it as the active service. Database migrations are NOT auto-rolled back — that's a manual revert with explicit confirmation.\n   104→- The pipeline spec version (`spec_version: \"1.0.0\"`) tracks the Digital Dash framework — bumping it requires the Digital Dash team's signoff (which is also SPY).\n   105→- `auto-commit.sh` is the canonical commit path. Skipping it for ad-hoc commits is a CLAUDE.md violation.\n   106→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"896edb10-d5e4-4e2d-8d2d-7fe02bdd0dae","uuid":"823e1e11-99da-4b4c-a7f2-7df92a9efd7a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomation/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/hyphae/HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY.md","content":"# HYPHA-INFRA-DEPLOY\n\n> HYPHA tag: `TA/INFRA`\n\n## Goal\n\nOwn the containerization, local-dev orchestration, AWS deployment, and Digital Dash CI/CD pipeline for Talent Agent. From `make up` to `./deploy/deploy.sh prod backend <sha>` to the production health check.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n- Backend `Dockerfile` (multi-stage; final image runs uvicorn)\n- Frontend `Dockerfile` + `nginx.conf` (builds React + serves `dist/`)\n- `docker-compose.yml` — local dev stack (postgres + redis + backend + frontend)\n- `Makefile` — common targets (`up`, `down`, `logs`, `seed`, `lint`, `test`)\n- `start.sh` / `stop.sh` — opinionated dev wrappers\n- `deploy/setup-aws.sh` — one-time bootstrap (ECR repos, ECS cluster, IAM, Secrets Manager entries)\n- `deploy/deploy.sh` — service deploy + rollback for backend/frontend across local/staging/prod\n- `deploy/ecs-task-def-backend.json` + `deploy/ecs-task-def-frontend.json` — Fargate task definitions\n- `digital-dash-pipeline.yml` — pipeline spec (lint → test → build → deploy-staging → health-check → deploy-prod with manual gate)\n- `.env.example` — env-var template\n- `.dockerignore` (if present; create if missing)\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Multi-region deployment (us-east-1 only)\n- Blue/green or canary (rolling update via ECS service update)\n- Database backups (RDS managed)\n- TLS cert provisioning (assume ACM cert exists, wired in ALB)\n- Container runtime alternatives (no Kubernetes; ECS Fargate only)\n- Pipeline alternatives (no GitHub Actions / CircleCI — Digital Dash is the pipeline)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- api-surface: backend exposes port 8000, `/health` returns `{status: \"ok\", version}`\n- review-dashboard: frontend builds to `dist/`, nginx serves on 80\n- Brief §0 (Stack lock) and §12 (Digital Dash result codes)\n- AWS Secrets Manager entries (out-of-band): `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`\n\n## Outputs (Deliverables)\n\nExisting files locked at HEAD:\n- `Dockerfile`\n- `frontend/Dockerfile`\n- `frontend/nginx.conf`\n- `docker-compose.yml`\n- `Makefile`\n- `start.sh`, `stop.sh`\n- `.env.example`\n- `deploy/setup-aws.sh`\n- `deploy/deploy.sh`\n- `deploy/ecs-task-def-backend.json`\n- `deploy/ecs-task-def-frontend.json`\n- `digital-dash-pipeline.yml`\n- `auto-commit.sh` (referenced as the per-task commit gate)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Local\n- [ ] `docker-compose up -d` brings up postgres, redis, backend, frontend with healthy containers\n- [ ] `make up` is equivalent to `docker-compose up -d`\n- [ ] `make down` stops all services cleanly\n- [ ] `make seed` runs `backend/seed.py` against the local DB\n- [ ] `make logs` tails container logs\n- [ ] Backend reaches `GET /health` returning `{status: \"ok\", …}` within 30s of `make up`\n- [ ] Frontend reaches `http://localhost:5173` and renders Landing\n\n### Docker images\n- [ ] Backend `Dockerfile` is multi-stage; runtime image is sub-500MB and runs as non-root\n- [ ] Backend image starts uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` by default\n- [ ] Frontend `Dockerfile` builds the React app with `npm ci && npm run build`, copies `dist/` into nginx, serves at port 80\n- [ ] Frontend nginx config falls back to `index.html` for unmatched routes (SPA history routing)\n\n### AWS / ECS\n- [ ] `deploy/setup-aws.sh` runs idempotently — re-running does not duplicate ECR repos or IAM roles\n- [ ] ECR repos `talent-agent-backend` and `talent-agent-frontend` exist after bootstrap\n- [ ] ECS cluster `vibespace-prod` exists with services `talent-agent-backend` and `talent-agent-frontend`\n- [ ] Task definitions pull `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET`, `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL` from AWS Secrets Manager (no plaintext secrets in JSON)\n- [ ] `./deploy/deploy.sh staging backend <git-sha>` builds, pushes to ECR, registers a new task def revision, updates the ECS service, waits for the deployment to stabilize\n- [ ] `./deploy/deploy.sh prod backend --rollback` reverts the service to the previous task def revision\n- [ ] `./deploy/deploy.sh local` is a `docker-compose up` shortcut\n\n### Digital Dash pipeline\n- [ ] `digital-dash-pipeline.yml` validates as YAML\n- [ ] Stages run in order: `lint` → `test` → `build` → `deploy-staging` → `health-check` → `deploy-prod`\n- [ ] `lint` runs `ruff check backend/`, `ruff format backend/ --check`, frontend `npm run lint`, and `bandit -ll` / `safety check` (warn-only)\n- [ ] `test` provisions postgres + redis services and runs `pytest tests/`\n- [ ] `build` is gated to `main` and `release/*` branches\n- [ ] `deploy-prod` requires manual approval from `spy@seanyoung.biz` with 24h timeout\n- [ ] `verify-prod` triggers an auto-rollback (backend + frontend) if `/health` is not `ok` post-deploy\n- [ ] Green pipeline auto-merges; red flags for human review; warned passes notify\n\n### Auto-commit\n- [ ] `./auto-commit.sh \"[TA] message\"` stages tracked changes, creates a commit prefixed with the stream tag, and refuses to commit secrets (`.env`, `credentials.json`)\n- [ ] `./auto-commit.sh` with no args auto-detects scope from changed files\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `vibespace-prod` ECS cluster is shared across VibeSpace products. Service names are product-scoped (`talent-agent-backend`, `talent-agent-frontend`).\n- Region is `us-east-1` everywhere. Changing region requires a brief amendment.\n- Secrets must NEVER appear in task definition JSON in plaintext — always `valueFrom` ARNs to Secrets Manager.\n- `health-check` stage uses `${STAGING_URL}` and a 5×10s retry pattern. Don't shorten the retry window — staging cold-start can take 30+ seconds.\n- `deploy-prod` manual gate is non-negotiable for this cultivation. Auto-merging to production without an approver is out of scope.\n- Rollback strategy: deploy.sh stores the previous task def revision; rollback re-registers it as the active service. Database migrations are NOT auto-rolled back — that's a manual revert with explicit confirmation.\n- The pipeline spec version (`spec_version: \"1.0.0\"`) tracks the Digital Dash framework — bumping it requires the Digital Dash team's signoff (which is also SPY).\n- `auto-commit.sh` is the canonical commit path. Skipping it for ad-hoc commits is a CLAUDE.md violation.\n","numLines":106,"startLine":1,"totalLines":106}}}}
